IMPORT `g2-art7-public-benefit`

-- g2-tests-art7.l4: tests of Article 7, every expected value decided from the Law's text before the module was run.
-- 7(1) binds the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court to 7(2) and 7(3); 5(5) binds every determiner to have regard to the guidance; 7(3)(b) makes one outcome a matter of law;
-- the Law does not say what follows from a breach, which is fork F2.10.

§ `Tests of Article 7`

GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`a determination by the Commissioner that provides public benefit` MEANS
    `a proper determination that the entity provides public benefit, made by` `the Commissioner`

§§ `Article 7(1): to whom paragraphs (2) and (3) apply`

-- src:203 | (1) Paragraphs (2) and (3) apply to the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court when determining the question of whether an entity provides or intends to provide public benefit, for the purpose of Article 5(1)(b).
#ASSERT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `the Commissioner` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `the Charity Tribunal` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `the court` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `any person` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `a registered charity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `a governor` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `an applicant for registration` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
