#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `the States` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
-- FORK F2.13.  Article 7(1) names the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court, and no member of staff; but Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) lets any function of the Commissioner be exercised on its behalf by a member
-- of staff, and a function so exercised is the Commissioner's.  First reading (taken): the duties go with it, so 7(2) and 7(3) bind the member of staff.
-- src:795 | (2) To the extent that any States’ employee (within the meaning of the Employment of States of Jersey Employees (Jersey) Law 2005), while made available under sub-paragraph (1), performs a function under the direction of the Commissioner, the employee is to be treated as a member of the Commissioner’s staff for the purposes of this Law.
