#ASSERT NOT `Arts 7(1) and 5(5) the Commissioner's staff are bound as the Commissioner is` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.13 read as B`

§§ `Article 7(2): regard to the comparison, and to undue restriction where benefit goes to a section of the public only`

-- src:204 | (2) The person determining the question must have regard to –
-- src:205 | (a) how any –
-- src:206 | (i) benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or any other persons (other than as members of the public), and
-- src:207 | (ii) disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public,
-- src:208 | in consequence of the entity exercising its functions, compares with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public in that consequence; and
-- src:209 | (b) if benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only, whether any condition on obtaining that benefit (including any charge or fee) is unduly restrictive.
-- (a) regard to the comparison; (b) not asked where benefit is not limited to a section of the public.
#ASSERT `Art 7(2) the determiner had the regard that Article 7(2) requires` `a determination by the Commissioner that provides public benefit`
-- (a) missed.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(2) the determiner had the regard that Article 7(2) requires` (`a determination that provides public benefit without regard to the comparison of 7(2)(a), made by` `the Commissioner`)
-- (b) required and missed.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(2) the determiner had the regard that Article 7(2) requires` (`a determination that provides public benefit for a section of the public without regard to undue restriction, made by` `the Commissioner`)
-- (b) required and had.
#ASSERT `Art 7(2) the determiner had the regard that Article 7(2) requires` (`a determination that provides public benefit for a section of the public with regard to undue restriction, made by` `the Commissioner`)

-- The duties as regulative rules.  A person that 7(1) binds has a standing duty; anyone else has none.
