§§ `Article 7(3): what the person determining must not do`

-- src:210 | (3) The person determining the question must not –
-- src:211 | (a) presume any particular charitable purpose to be for the public benefit; or
-- src:212 | (b) treat one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons as being a section of the public, and accordingly must not treat an entity that benefits only such a person or persons as providing public benefit.
-- (a) presuming a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit.
#ASSERT `Art 7(3)(a) the determination did not presume a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit` `a determination by the Commissioner that provides public benefit`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(3)(a) the determination did not presume a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit` (`a determination that provides public benefit by presuming a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit, made by` `the Commissioner`)
-- (b) treating identified natural persons as a section of the public, and so treating an entity that benefits only them as providing public benefit.
#ASSERT `Art 7(3)(b) the determination did not treat identified natural persons as a section of the public` `a determination by the Commissioner that provides public benefit`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(3)(b) the determination did not treat identified natural persons as a section of the public` (`a determination that treats identified natural persons as a section of the public, made by` `the Commissioner`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(3)(b) the determination did not treat identified natural persons as a section of the public` (`a determination that provides public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified natural persons, made by` `the Commissioner`)
-- An entity that benefits only identified natural persons, found NOT to provide public benefit, is correctly treated.
#ASSERT `Art 7(3)(b) the determination did not treat identified natural persons as a section of the public` (`a determination that does not provide public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified natural persons, made by` `the Commissioner`)
-- The combined test.
#ASSERT `Art 7(3) the determination is permitted` `a determination by the Commissioner that provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(3) the determination is permitted` (`a determination that provides public benefit by presuming a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit, made by` `the Charity Tribunal`) `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(3) the determination is permitted` (`a determination that provides public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified natural persons, made by` `the court`) `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
-- 7(1) does not bind a person who is not the Commissioner, the tribunal or the court: 7(3) is satisfied vacuously.
#ASSERT `Art 7(3) the determination is permitted` (`a determination that provides public benefit by presuming a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit, made by` `any person`) `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 7(3) the determination is permitted` (`a determination that provides public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified natural persons, made by` `a registered charity`) `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`

-- FORK F2.13: a determination by a member of the Commissioner's staff that treats identified natural persons as a section of the public.  First reading (taken): not permitted; second: permitted.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(3) the determination is permitted` (`a determination that provides public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified natural persons, made by` `a member of the Commissioner's staff`) `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 7(3) the determination is permitted` (`a determination that provides public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified natural persons, made by` `a member of the Commissioner's staff`) `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.13 read as B`
#ASSERT `Art 7(3) the determination is permitted` (`a determination by the Commissioner that provides public benefit`) `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.13 read as B`

-- The prohibitions as regulative rules: holding without end, breached by the act, binding only those 7(1) binds.
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 7(3)(a)
