§§ `Article 7 with Article 5(5): whether the determination complies with the duties on its maker`

-- src:157 | (5) Any person, in determining whether an entity meets the charity test, must have regard to the guidance, and the Commissioner, the tribunal, a registered charity and a governor of a registered charity must have regard to the guidance when performing any other of their functions under this Law to which the guidance is relevant.
#ASSERT `Art 7 the determination complies with the duties on its maker` `a determination by the Commissioner that provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
-- 5(5) binds every determiner: a determination without regard to the guidance does not comply, whoever made it.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the determination complies with the duties on its maker` (`a determination that provides public benefit without regard to the guidance, made by` `the Commissioner`) `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the determination complies with the duties on its maker` (`a determination that provides public benefit without regard to the guidance, made by` `any person`) `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
-- 7(2) and 7(3) bind only the three: a person who is not one of them need not have the 7(2) regard nor avoid the presumption.
#ASSERT `Art 7 the determination complies with the duties on its maker` (`a determination that provides public benefit without regard to the comparison of 7(2)(a), made by` `a registered charity`) `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 7 the determination complies with the duties on its maker` (`a determination that provides public benefit by presuming a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit, made by` `a governor`) `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the determination complies with the duties on its maker` (`a determination that provides public benefit without regard to the comparison of 7(2)(a), made by` `the court`) `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the determination complies with the duties on its maker` (`a determination that provides public benefit by presuming a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit, made by` `the Charity Tribunal`) `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`

-- FORK F2.13: a member of staff determines without the 7(2)(a) regard.  First reading (taken): the determination does not comply; second reading: it does, as for anyone else Article 7(1) does not name.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the determination complies with the duties on its maker` (`a determination that provides public benefit without regard to the comparison of 7(2)(a), made by` `a member of the Commissioner's staff`) `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 7 the determination complies with the duties on its maker` (`a determination that provides public benefit without regard to the comparison of 7(2)(a), made by` `a member of the Commissioner's staff`) `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.13 read as B`
-- Staff are bound by 5(5) on both readings when determining: a determination without regard to the guidance does not comply, whoever made it.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the determination complies with the duties on its maker` (`a determination that provides public benefit without regard to the guidance, made by` `a member of the Commissioner's staff`) `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the determination complies with the duties on its maker` (`a determination that provides public benefit without regard to the guidance, made by` `a member of the Commissioner's staff`) `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.13 read as B`

§§ `Article 5(1)(b) with Article 7: does the entity provide public benefit?`

GIVETH AN Entity
`an unregistered entity` MEANS `a G2 entity with these purposes` EMPTY
GIVETH AN Entity
`an applicant entity` MEANS `a G2 applicant with these purposes` EMPTY
GIVETH AN Entity
`a registered charity entity` MEANS `a G2 registered charity with these purposes` EMPTY

-- src:149 | (b) in giving effect to those purposes, it provides (or, in the case of an applicant, provides or intends to provide) public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree.
-- A proper determination answers with its finding.
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an unregistered entity` (`a proper determination that the entity provides public benefit, made by` `the Commissioner`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an unregistered entity` (`a proper determination that the entity does not provide public benefit, made by` `the Commissioner`)
-- "Intends to provide" counts for an applicant only.
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an applicant entity` (`a proper determination that the entity intends to provide public benefit, made by` `the Commissioner`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an unregistered entity` (`a proper determination that the entity intends to provide public benefit, made by` `the Commissioner`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `a registered charity entity` (`a proper determination that the entity intends to provide public benefit, made by` `the Commissioner`)
-- An applicant that provides already counts too.
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an applicant entity` (`a proper determination that the entity provides public benefit, made by` `the court`)
-- Anyone may determine, and a lay finding stands if made with regard to the guidance.
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `a registered charity entity` (`a proper determination that the entity provides public benefit, made by` `a governor`)

-- src:210 | (3) The person determining the question must not –
-- src:211 | (a) presume any particular charitable purpose to be for the public benefit; or
-- src:212 | (b) treat one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons as being a section of the public, and accordingly must not treat an entity that benefits only such a person or persons as providing public benefit.
-- 7(3)(b): the Commissioner, the tribunal or the court must not treat an entity that benefits only identified natural persons as providing public benefit, whatever the finding and whatever F2.10 says.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that provides public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified natural persons, made by` `the Commissioner`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that provides public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified natural persons, made by` `the Charity Tribunal`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.10 read as B` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that provides public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified natural persons, made by` `the court`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.10 read as C` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that provides public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified natural persons, made by` `the Commissioner`)
-- 7(1) does not bind a person who is not one of the three: such a person's finding stands.
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that provides public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified natural persons, made by` `a governor`)

-- FORK F2.13, the discriminating case (an independent test author's case): a member of the Commissioner's staff, authorized under Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3), finds that an entity that benefits only one
-- named natural person provides public benefit.  First reading (taken): the staff finding is the Commissioner's, 7(3)(b) binds it, and the entity does not provide public benefit.  Second reading: Article 7(1)
-- does not name staff, so the finding stands.
