#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that provides public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified natural persons, made by` `a member of the Commissioner's staff`)
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.13 read as B` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that provides public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified natural persons, made by` `a member of the Commissioner's staff`)
-- A staff finding of public benefit that breaches nothing stands on both readings.
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an unregistered entity` (`a proper determination that the entity provides public benefit, made by` `a member of the Commissioner's staff`)
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.13 read as B` `an unregistered entity` (`a proper determination that the entity provides public benefit, made by` `a member of the Commissioner's staff`)
-- A staff finding that presumes a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit is a breach of 7(3)(a) on the first reading, which F2.10 (first reading) refuses; on the second the finding stands.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that provides public benefit by presuming a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit, made by` `a member of the Commissioner's staff`) BECAUSE "a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker does not answer the question whether the entity provides public benefit"
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.13 read as B` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that provides public benefit by presuming a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit, made by` `a member of the Commissioner's staff`)

-- FORK F2.10, the discriminating case: the Commissioner presumed a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit (7(3)(a)) and found that the entity provides public benefit.
-- The Law does not say what follows, so the first reading (taken) refuses; the second lets the finding stand; the third treats the entity as not providing public benefit.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that provides public benefit by presuming a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit, made by` `the Commissioner`) BECAUSE "a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker does not answer the question whether the entity provides public benefit"
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.10 read as B` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that provides public benefit by presuming a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit, made by` `the Commissioner`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.10 read as C` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that provides public benefit by presuming a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit, made by` `the Commissioner`)
-- The same on the other breaches: no regard to the comparison (the court), no regard to undue restriction (the tribunal), no regard to the guidance (anyone), treating identified persons as a section (the Commissioner).
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that provides public benefit without regard to the comparison of 7(2)(a), made by` `the court`) BECAUSE "a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker does not answer the question whether the entity provides public benefit"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that provides public benefit for a section of the public without regard to undue restriction, made by` `the Charity Tribunal`) BECAUSE "a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker does not answer the question whether the entity provides public benefit"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that provides public benefit without regard to the guidance, made by` `a registered charity`) BECAUSE "a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker does not answer the question whether the entity provides public benefit"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that treats identified natural persons as a section of the public, made by` `the Commissioner`) BECAUSE "a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker does not answer the question whether the entity provides public benefit"
-- The compliant versions of the section-of-the-public case answer.
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an unregistered entity` (`a determination that provides public benefit for a section of the public with regard to undue restriction, made by` `the Charity Tribunal`)

§§ `Article 7(4): guidance on public benefit`

-- src:213 | (4) The guidance published by the Commissioner under Article 5(4), must in particular give guidance on the determination of the question of whether an entity provides or intends to provide public benefit.
#ASSERT `Art 7(4) the guidance published under Article 5(4) gives guidance on public benefit` (LIST `the determination of whether an entity meets the charity test`, `the determination of whether an entity provides or intends to provide public benefit`)
#ASSERT `Art 7(4) the guidance published under Article 5(4) gives guidance on public benefit` (LIST `the determination of whether an entity provides or intends to provide public benefit`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(4) the guidance published under Article 5(4) gives guidance on public benefit` (LIST `the determination of whether an entity meets the charity test`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(4) the guidance published under Article 5(4) gives guidance on public benefit` EMPTY
